From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2562: reset the amplifier at component probe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Copyright (c) 2026 Alp Lab AB
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0

The driver's register cache starts from the POR defaults, including
PAGE_CTRL = 0, but nothing puts the silicon in that state.  When the part
was not power-cycled -- a warm reboot with SD_N held high, which is what
happens on the E1M-X-EVK where SD_N is one shared net for both TAS2563
amps -- it keeps the previous kernel's book, page and configuration.
regmap then skips the page-select write (the cached selector already
reads 0), so page-0 writes land in whatever page was left selected (page
2, after any Digital Volume change), and cached writes that match the
stale defaults are dropped as no-ops.

Seen on an E1M-V2M103 bench board after `reboot -f`: PB_CFG1 kept the
previous boot's amplifier level while the cache said otherwise, so
"Amp Gain Volume" writes silently did nothing, and the TDM slot width
set by set_tdm_slot never reached TDM_CFG2.

In the component probe -- at card bind, after every instance sharing
SD_N has probed and released it -- wait for the part to leave shutdown,
select book 0 / page 0 with the cache bypassed, issue SW_RESET, and wait
for the reset to complete.

Upstream-Status: Pending [generic driver fix; no SoM-specific code]

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 
 #include "tas2562.h"
 
+#define TAS2562_BOOK_CTRL	TAS2562_REG(0, 0x7f)
+
 #define TAS2562_FORMATS (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |\
 			 SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE)
 
@@ -384,12 +386,40 @@
 static int tas2562_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 {
 	struct tas2562_data *tas2562 = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
+	int ret;
 
 	tas2562->component = component;
 
 	if (tas2562->sdz_gpio)
 		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(tas2562->sdz_gpio, 1);
 
+	/*
+	 * SD_N may be shared between amplifiers and is not necessarily
+	 * cycled by a warm reboot, so the device can still hold the
+	 * previous kernel's book, page and configuration.  The register
+	 * cache starts from the POR defaults -- including PAGE_CTRL = 0,
+	 * which makes regmap skip the page-select write -- so accesses
+	 * would land in whatever page was left selected.  Select book 0 /
+	 * page 0 with the cache bypassed and issue a software reset so the
+	 * silicon matches the cache.  This runs at card bind rather than in
+	 * the I2C probe, so every instance sharing SD_N has released it;
+	 * give the device time to leave shutdown first.
+	 */
+	usleep_range(2000, 3000);
+	regcache_cache_bypass(tas2562->regmap, true);
+	ret = regmap_write(tas2562->regmap, TAS2562_PAGE_CTRL, 0x00);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_write(tas2562->regmap, TAS2562_BOOK_CTRL, 0x00);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_write(tas2562->regmap, TAS2562_SW_RESET, 0x01);
+	regcache_cache_bypass(tas2562->regmap, false);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(tas2562->dev, "failed to reset device: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+	/* Allow the reset to complete before the first cached access. */
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
